00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:06.899
Speaker 1: Let's talk to why don't we go to
Andrew from Miami.

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:09.030
Andrew, you're on the air.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.220
Hi, David.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.220
I can.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:17.830
Speaker 6: Hey, so I was curious what your
opinion was of Nancy Pelosi recently investing

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.220
10 million dollars in Microsoft.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.840
Speaker 1: I didn't know that she did what
she bought 10 million dollars worth of of

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.070
Microsoft stock.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.179
Speaker 6: Correct, around a month ago, she
invested upwards of 10 million dollars in

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:32.680
Microsoft stock, and then shortly after that,
Microsoft received a government contract for

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.630
a pretty large sum of money and then the stock
went up.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:41.530
Speaker 1: You know, there is a lot of stuff
about Nancy Pelosi that is that is untrue.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:47.240
And I want to be careful because there's a
rumor that Nancy Pelosi is worth one hundred

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.670
and ninety six million.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.390
But it seems she's really only worth five
million dollars.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:57.120
So when you're telling me she invested 10
million, I just I haven't heard that.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.120
And I'm just unsure about that.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.570
I think her husband is quite wealthy.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:04.670
I don't know, because of all of the incorrect
stuff.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.670
I just don't know.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.729
Speaker 6: Yeah, her husband just owns a major
investment firm, so he has ties to Wall Street

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:14.479
and then she directly acts on legislation
that would affect the stocks that she invest

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:15.479
in.

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:20.340
Speaker 1: Yeah, I mean, listen, I've come
out before and I've said that it is too easy

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.810
to violate the STOCK Act for members of the
House and Senate.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.170
There are real questions about that being
not nearly regulated enough.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.569
And I apply that to Republicans as much as
Democrats specifically, Nancy, investing 10

00:01:32.569 --> 00:01:34.869
million went as far as I know, her net worth
is five.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:36.970
I just I just don't know about that.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.729
Speaker 6: Gotcha.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:43.719
I mean, just in light of her recent comments
as well, after the show trial, it just seems

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:44.719
like she's a liability.

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.210
Speaker 1: Democrats and her comments about
the showband thing were for people who don't

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.179
know, she said something like, I want to thank
George Floyd for sacrificing himself in the

00:01:52.179 --> 00:01:54.450
name of justice or whatever.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.439
It's like, whoa, hold on a second.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:58.100
He didn't he didn't sacrifice himself.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.510
And that's really strange language.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:04.039
And it seems an insanely and that was just
a major faux pas.

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:05.600
Speaker 6: I agree.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.410
So it seems like she's a liability to Dems
and almost seems like she wants Republicans

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.700
to win in the midterms.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.080
Speaker 1: I don't think she wants Republicans
to win.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.020
I just think she's making missteps.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.820
Why would she want Republicans to win?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:22.130
Speaker 6: It would lengthen her ability to
continue fighting for corporations as opposed

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.980
to actually people's interests now.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.510
Speaker 1: Now, that doesn't ring, right?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.120
I don't think so.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.200
I think Nancy Pelosi certainly to some degree
is focused on herself.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.490
But I have no reason to think she wants Republicans
to win.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.490
Speaker 3: Interesting.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.570
Thanks so much, David.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.060
Speaker 1: All right, pleasure.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.540
Great to hear from you.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:43.340
OK, let's see who else we can hear from because
we really have been having some beautiful

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.040
phone calls today.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.100
Excellent, excellent calls.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.060
Let's talk to Lucas from Hendersonville.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.730
Where is Hendersonville, by the way?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.430
Speaker 3: Hey, it's north of Nashville.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.190
Speaker 1: Oh, OK.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.190
Hendersonville, Tennessee.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.190
Very beautiful.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.270
Speaker 3: OK.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.270
Yes, sir.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.270
Thank you.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:10.730
My question to you is that there is about
10 million illegal immigrants in the U.S.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:18.370
What steps should Biden take to help accommodate
those people and to the American society that

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.370
we have to do?

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:24.580
Speaker 1: Well, I think you have to kind
of go in in stages.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.400
And the first thing is DACA has to be dealt
with.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.440
There has to be a permanent solution on DACA.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:38.430
It's hard for me to to lay out a full policy
sequence because so much of it depends on

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.400
if, how and when DACA is dealt with.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.690
I do think that a clear path to citizenship
should be put in place.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:50.870
I mean, I don't have any any unique particular
view on this.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:57.400
It's it's what you know, I like what people
like Roxana have talked about on immigration

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:06.350
and, you know, Congressman Ruben Gallego and
others just just kind of a just reasonable

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:11.830
system where we're treating people with respect
and we're understanding that the vast majority

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:17.430
of undocumented immigrants are here working,
paying into systems and raising families,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.430
et cetera.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.320
Yeah, I don't have anything groundbreaking
on that.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.900
Speaker 3: Thank you.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.710
Speaker 1: My pleasure.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.349
Appreciate the phone call.

00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:29.930
OK, that is going to close today's call session.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:35.819
